  "result": "`drv.motion.turning_right` passes the gate with **OK** on the second of the 6 allowed runs (3 witnesses, 2 names, reads 2 atoms).\n\n**Body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/turning_right.lean`):\n```lean\n.and\n  (.not (.derived \"drv_motion_at_rest\" [aA] [pSpeedTolerance]))\n  (.cmp (.measure \"kin_yaw_rate\" [aA]) .le (.neg pYawTolerance))\n```\nIt is the contract's two elements, checked at the observation being judged: the road user is not at rest, and its yaw rate is at or below minus the yaw tolerance. It doesn't read the turn indicator or the road's shape, so following a bend to the right counts too, as the contract says. The contract's words fix the body exactly, so there are no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/turning_right.lean`): the yaw tolerance is 2 deg/s and the speed tolerance 0.1 m/s. One car moves at 8 m/s over three instants one second apart.\n- **holds:** in an intersection, yaw rate −25 deg/s.\n- **fails:** on a straight roadway, yaw rate 0.5 deg/s.\n- **blind:** the `holds` trace with `kin.yaw_rate` masked.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **`WITNESS_FAIL`.** The trace check rejected `holds` and `fails` because the car kept the same heading while a nonzero yaw rate said it was turning. I changed each scene's heading to a unit vector that turns between instants about as far as the yaw rate says. The body did not change.\n2. **OK.**\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
